Template: tt-bio-demo-weights/download
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Download the model weights now (6.9 GB)?
 The booth needs two artifacts before it can fold anything:
 protenix-v2.pt (1.86 GB) and the CCD molecule library mols.tar (1.85 GB).
 Together that is about 3.7 GB.
 .
 It also needs three more before it can answer an affinity question
 ("does this ligand bind this protein?"): nesso1's affinity head
 (165 MB), its own CCD molecule dict (413 MB), and the ESM-2 protein
 encoder its featurizer runs (2.6 GB) -- about 3.2 GB more, for 6.9 GB
 total. A booth running with --no-questions, or with only one
 Tenstorrent chip (which never reserves a Q&A worker), does not need
 these three at all, but a failure fetching them will not fail this
 install either way -- see the log for what landed.
 .
 THE VENUE IS OFFLINE. This has to happen before the machine leaves for the
 conference, which is why it is offered at install time -- but 6.9 GB is not
 something an unattended install should start on its own, so the default is
 to decline and the exact commands are printed instead.
 .
 The download is resumable and is fetched through tt-bio's own Hugging Face
 client, so an interrupted attempt continues rather than restarting.
